<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo, Scancem set up Singapore cement venture.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo, Scancem set up Singapore cement venture.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Corp and Norwegian cement maker Scancem have set up a joint venture in Singapore to market cement in Asia, a Japanese business daily reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The new firm is capitalised at 200 million yen and equally owned by Sumitomo and Scancem, the daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said.</p>
<p>The joint venture will purchase cement from major producers in Japan, South Korea and Thailand. It aims to market about three million tonnes of cement per year and expects sales of 20 billion yen in five years' time, the paper said.</p>
</text>
